The 2024–25 season was the 97th season in the history of Real Valladolid. In addition to the domestic league, the team participated in the [[Copa del Rey]].

== Summary ==
On 29 May, Croatian Stanko Juric's loan from Parma was made permanent, signing a three-season contract.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.elnortedecastilla.es/realvalladolid/real-valladolid-anuncia-continuidad-stanko-juric-2027-20240529112038-nt.html|title=El Real Valladolid anuncia la continuidad de Stanko Juric hasta 2027|first=Arturo|last=Posada|date=29 May 2024|website=El Norte de Castilla}}</ref> On 31 May, Real Valladolid exercised their purchase option and included Senegalese Amat Ndiaye, tying him to the club until 2027.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.marca.com/futbol/mallorca/2024/05/27/6654e63ee2704ed37f8b45b3.html|title=El Mallorca hace caja con Amath Ndiaye... que firmará con el Valladolid hasta 2027|date=27 May 2024|website=MARCA}}</ref>

